 rigin: var(--origin-x) var(--origin-y)\; } About the Book In Confessions o
 f a Recovering Engineer: Transportation for a Strong Town\, author and urb
 anist Charles L. Marohn\, Jr. delivers an accessible and engaging explorat
 ion of America's transportation system. He lays bare the reasons why trans
 it no longer works as it once did\, and envisions how to modernize transpo
 rtation to better serve local communities. In the book\, you’ll discover
  real-world examples of poor transportation design choices that have had d
 ramatic and tragic effects. You'll also find examples of design improvemen
 ts that have revitalized communities and improved safety. #block-f1e6baa8d
